Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Review: the seam-conforming path still refuses a cavity
 along the wall; only true wall edges count

At np 3 on the seam-conforming path (top at 60 degrees, gaps 0.31 and 0.61
cells) one rank's fill ring held a 5.4-cell chord across the band, and gmsh
spun on it while the other ranks waited in the gather; at np 2 the outcome
depended on the partition. Until that path is sound, it refuses a cavity
along the wall as before, through the placement's failure gather, so no rank
reaches gmsh: the message names seams='gather', the default, which places it.

The gathered path's wall edges now also need both ends to be true wall
vertices, so a partition seam's edge can never count as wall.

tests/parallel/test_0904 (np 2-3): the gathered path places both gaps and the
seam-conforming path refuses them with the remedy, alike on every rank.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
